## Image Processing Techniques

### 1. Median Filtering

Median filtering reduces unwanted noise by replacing each pixel with the median value of its surrounding neighborhood.

A 3×3 kernel is used as the initial configuration.

### 2. Histogram Equalization

Histogram equalization improves image contrast by redistributing pixel intensity values.

It can make differences between dark and bright regions more visible, although it may also enhance unwanted noise.

### 3. Canny Edge Detection

Canny edge detection identifies changes in image intensity and highlights important boundaries.

The initial threshold values are:

- Lower threshold: 50
- Upper threshold: 150

Different threshold values are tested to compare edge detection results.

## Experimental Evaluation

The project includes experiments with different parameter settings:

| Technique | Parameters |
|---|---|
| Median Filtering | 3×3 and 5×5 kernels |
| Canny Edge Detection | 30–100 and 100–200 thresholds |

The resulting images are compared to evaluate noise reduction, contrast enhancement, and edge detection.

