## Results

The processing pipeline produces intermediate and final outputs:

- Noise-reduced CT scan.
- Contrast-enhanced CT scan.
- Canny edge detection result.
- Comparison of different filter sizes and threshold values.

The results demonstrate how classical image-processing techniques can improve the visibility of image structures and highlight boundaries.

## Limitations

- Histogram equalization may enhance unwanted noise.
- Canny edge detection may detect boundaries of the heart and other structures along with the lungs.
- Edge detection does not provide complete lung segmentation.
- Results depend on image quality and parameter settings.

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates the use of classical image-processing techniques for CT scan enhancement and edge detection. Median filtering, histogram equalization, and Canny edge detection are combined to reduce noise, improve contrast, and highlight important boundaries.

The experimental comparison helps identify suitable parameter settings for the given image.

